<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Reference performance of the <span id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span> (mean <math id="S5.T1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> s.e., <math id="S5.T1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}10</annotation></semantics></math> independent runs; per-task mean–max checkpointing per <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Evaluation &amp; Statistical Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Details ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) versus the single fixed <math id="S5.T1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GOOD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖮𝖮𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GOOD}</annotation></semantics></math> checkpoint. Because it is a single checkpoint chosen once across seeds rather than per task, it can sit below the <span id="S5.T1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span> mean on some tasks.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-task mean-max over checkpoints.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each training method<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              Either <span id="footnote2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span>, or a pair of decoding strategy from <a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" title="Decoding Strategies. ‣ 4.1 Synthetic Corpus Generation ‣ 4 Training on Synthetic Data ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and bad model setting from <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 The 𝖡𝖠𝖣 and 𝖦𝖮𝖮𝖣 Models ‣ 4 Training on Synthetic Data ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></span></span></span> <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, benchmark task <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and initialization seed <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we save checkpoints every 500 steps and select the best checkpoint independently per <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,t,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,t,s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{m,t,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{m,t,s}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of saved checkpoints over the steps, and <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m,t,s}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m,t,s}(c)</annotation></semantics></math> the task score at checkpoint <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. For higher-is-better tasks, we set</p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}_{m,t,s}\mathrel{\overset{\raisebox{-0.75346pt}{{def}}}{=}}\arg\max_{c\in\mathcal{C}_{m,t,s}}S_{m,t,s}(c)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mpadded voffset="-0.8pt"><mtext mathsize="0.700em">def</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}_{m,t,s}\mathrel{\overset{\raisebox{-0.75346pt}{{def}}}{=}}\arg\max_{c\in\mathcal{C}_{m,t,s}}S_{m,t,s}(c),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">while for perplexity we take <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\min</annotation></semantics></math>. The selected checkpoint <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}_{m,t,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}_{m,t,s}</annotation></semantics></math> is then evaluated. This procedure estimates the best attainable performance per task under the fixed training budget and avoids coupling to a single global checkpoint.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Paired bootstrap for statistical significance.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluation of checkpoint <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}_{m,t,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}_{m,t,s}</annotation></semantics></math> for task t yields per-example outcomes <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{m,t,s,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{m,t,s,i}</annotation></semantics></math> for examples <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use paired bootstrap with <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1000</annotation></semantics></math> resamples to calculate confidence intervals. For each <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,s)</annotation></semantics></math> and bootstrap draw <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, sample the index-set <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{(b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{(b)}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with replacement from <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,N_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,N_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the <em id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same</em> <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{(b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{(b)}</annotation></semantics></math> to all methods (pairing). We average out uncertainty over the seeds:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{y}^{(b)}_{m,t,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{y}^{(b)}_{m,t,s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{t}}\sum_{i\in I^{(b)}}y_{m,t,s,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{t}}\sum_{i\in I^{(b)}}y_{m,t,s,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu^{(b)}_{m,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu^{(b)}_{m,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\bar{y}^{(b)}_{m,t,s}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\bar{y}^{(b)}_{m,t,s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As in (<a href="#S5.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Paired bootstrap for statistical significance. ‣ 5.3 Evaluation &amp; Statistical Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Details ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}^{(b)}_{m,t,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}^{(b)}_{m,t,s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean for tasks with per-example scalar scores (e.g., BLiMP, EWoK). For metrics with task-specific aggregations (e.g., Perplexity or Reading), we substitute the appropriate aggregation function and proceed identically.
For a comparison of two methods <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we form the bootstrap difference distribution</p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(b)}_{t}=\mu^{(b)}_{m_{1},t}-\mu^{(b)}_{m_{2},t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(b)}_{t}=\mu^{(b)}_{m_{1},t}-\mu^{(b)}_{m_{2},t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We compute 95% confidence intervals via the percentile method, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CI}_{95}=[\mathrm{pct}_{2.5},\,\mathrm{pct}_{97.5}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>CI</mi><mn>95</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>pct</mi><mn>2.5</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>pct</mi><mn>97.5</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CI}_{95}=[\mathrm{pct}_{2.5},\,\mathrm{pct}_{97.5}]</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Delta^{(b)}_{t}\}_{b=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Delta^{(b)}_{t}\}_{b=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. A difference is deemed significant if <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\notin\mathrm{CI}_{95}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>CI</mi><mn>95</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\notin\mathrm{CI}_{95}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compute one-sided <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values in the direction of the observed effect using the estimator on the bootstrap differences <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Delta_{t}^{(b)}\}_{b=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Delta_{t}^{(b)}\}_{b=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>: for higher-is-better tasks with <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Delta}_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Delta}_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p=\frac{1+\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{I}\{\Delta_{t}^{(b)}\leq 0\}}{B+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p=\frac{1+\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{I}\{\Delta_{t}^{(b)}\leq 0\}}{B+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and if <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Delta}_{t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Delta}_{t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> use <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math> instead. For lower-is-better metrics we swap the inequality accordingly.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Aggregate reporting.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For tables and figures, we bold the best method per benchmark and mark significant improvements/degradations relative to the <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span>. We report, for each method <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and task <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the bootstrap mean <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{m,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{m,t}</annotation></semantics></math> and standard-error.</p>
<table id="S5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\mu}_{m,t}\;=\;\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mu^{(b)}_{m,t},\quad\widehat{\mathrm{SE}}_{m,t}=\frac{\sigma_{m,t}}{\sqrt{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>SE</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mi>B</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\mu}_{m,t}\;=\;\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mu^{(b)}_{m,t},\quad\widehat{\mathrm{SE}}_{m,t}=\frac{\sigma_{m,t}}{\sqrt{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This analysis serves to estimate the maximum achievable performance for each method, on each task, given the training setup.
Our aggregating metric <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\Delta\mathrm{REL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>REL</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\Delta\mathrm{REL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean relative performance, across all tasks except Perplexity, vs. the <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span>—i.e., it is the average proportional change given in percentages.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Results</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span><span id="S6.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span> Performance</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.T1" title="In Benchmarks. ‣ 5.3 Evaluation &amp; Statistical Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Details ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the performance of our reference points, the <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GOOD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖮𝖮𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GOOD}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span> results. Recall that the <span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span> row reports the mean <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> s.e. over <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}10</annotation></semantics></math> independent runs under our per-task bootstrapped mean–max evaluation (<a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Evaluation &amp; Statistical Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Details ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>). In contrast, the <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GOOD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖮𝖮𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GOOD}</annotation></semantics></math> model is a <em id="S6.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single</em> checkpoint selected once, across seeds, using the selection procedure described in <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Model Architecture &amp; Training Setup ‣ 5 Experimental Details ‣ Contrastive Decoding for Synthetic Data Generationin Low-Resource Language Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>. As such <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GOOD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖮𝖮𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GOOD}</annotation></semantics></math> is broadly representative of a strong model but sits slightly below the <span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Baseline</span> mean on some tasks (e.g., Perplexity, BLiMP Supplement) because it cannot adapt per task. We use this fixed checkpoint as the <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GOOD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖮𝖮𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GOOD}</annotation></semantics></math> model in all subsequent synthetic corpora and comparisons.</p>
</div>
</section>
